From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:58:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 76/91] Stacking penalties through dogma

A module's or rig's multiplier on an attribute that isn't stackable
(dgmAttributeTypes.stackable = 0: resists, speed, damage, tracking, range,
scan resolution, signature and so on) is now stacking penalised, as the
client shows it. The n-th strongest one counts 0.5 ^ ((n / 2.2229)^2):
100%, 87%, 57%, 28%, 11%...

- PreMul, PreDiv, PostMul, PostDiv and PostPercent each have their own chain
  per item and attribute, as in dogma. So a Damage Control (PreMul) doesn't
  stack with hardeners and EANMs (PostPercent).
- Bonuses and penalties are ranked apart.
- Skills, implants, boosters, the hull, subsystems, charges and scripts, and
  system effects aren't penalised.
- Removing a module takes its exact multiplier back out of the chain, even if
  its own value changed meanwhile (overheat).

Webs, damps, TDs and painters were already penalised through their own code.
